        "original_id": "b62d8afe-78da-5dad-9359-760fcdb3bd75",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jimmy McNatt\n- Organizations: Oklahoma Sooners men's basketball, University of Oklahoma, Phillips 66, AAU\n- Concepts: All-American honors, nickname origins\n\nFacts:\n- The Oklahoma Sooners men's basketball team represents the University of Oklahoma in men's NCAA Division I basketball.\n- In the 1937–38 season, sportswriters used the term “Boy Scats” to describe Jimmy McNatt’s fast-breaking, sophomore-led Oklahoma Sooners basketball team.\n- Jimmy McNatt’s nickname “Scat” McNatt was traced to the term “Boy Scats.”\n- Jimmy McNatt was a two-time All-American at Oklahoma in 1939 and 1940.\n- Jimmy McNatt was a four-time AAU All-American for Phillips 66 in 1943, 1944, 1945, and 1946.",
